{"chapter": "spaces-groupoids", "node_kind": "example", "parent_tag": "06P7", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$B \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$n \\geq 1$", "MATH_0003": "$$\n\\det : \\text{GL}_{n, B} \\longrightarrow \\mathbf{G}_{m, B}\n$$", "MATH_0004": "$B$", "MATH_0005": "$S$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{section-notation}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{groupoids-example-determinant}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{example}\n\\label{example-determinant}\n", "suffix": "\\end{example}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:99f51d35f3777dd89c215b1b5d41636cfaff8e9e950a1a0bccc932a217391409", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:043ab796fd797a31e556c6869937f6cf47015c2fba8fb9290b0f73aea7ef6652", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> as in Section <REF_0001>.\nLet <MATH_0002>.\nThe determinant defines a morphism of group algebraic spaces\n<MATH_0003>\nover <MATH_0004>. It is the base change of the determinant morphism\nover <MATH_0005> from\nGroupoids, Example <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b95b74ea3bc961be636423085b47136e3e83b101149cc9524fe525968ff89a4a", "unit_id": "tag:043N:statement"}
{"chapter": "spaces-groupoids", "node_kind": "example", "parent_tag": "06P7", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$B \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$G$", "MATH_0003": "$T$", "MATH_0004": "$B$", "MATH_0005": "$T \\to G$", "MATH_0006": "$T$", "MATH_0007": "$G$", "MATH_0008": "$$\nG_B = B \\times_S G_S\n$$", "MATH_0009": "$B$", "MATH_0010": "$G_S$", "OWNARGEND_0001": "]\n\\label{example-constant-group}\n", "REF_0001": "\\ref{section-notation}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{groupoids-example-constant-group}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{example}[", "suffix": "\\end{example}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:acb7e183b2be7e30e22de1770ecb40d00227c6d6944a2ba44ba8b2f085857776", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d6fa30353162da679624ce903de5a1ce0687e3d27dd30c22e9470891c8e6af9e", "source_text": "Constant group algebraic space<OWNARGEND_0001>Let <MATH_0001> as in Section <REF_0001>.\nLet <MATH_0002> be an abstract group. Consider the functor\nwhich associates to any scheme <MATH_0003> over <MATH_0004> the group\nof locally constant maps <MATH_0005> (where <MATH_0006> has the Zariski topology\nand <MATH_0007> the discrete topology). This is representable by the\ngroup algebraic space\n<MATH_0008>\nover <MATH_0009>. Here <MATH_0010> is the constant group scheme introduced in\nGroupoids, Example <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:639c32a1fc49589e82c009979abec48e893d054c78692a714a74d814f5c6c882", "unit_id": "tag:043O:statement"}
